---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Now"
  description="What I am currently building, learning, exploring, and reading. Replace this page as focus changes."
  canonicalPath="/now"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <p class="text-faint font-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase">Now</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-serif text-4xl tracking-tight">Currently</h1>
    <p class="text-faint mt-4 text-sm">
      This page is a snapshot of current focus. It will go stale; that is
      expected. Edit
      <code class="font-mono text-xs">src/pages/now.astro</code> when things change.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight">Currently building</h2>
    <p class="text-muted mt-3">
      This site: a content-first home for writing, notes, projects, and
      experiments. <!-- replace -->
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight">Currently learning</h2>
    <p class="text-muted mt-3">
      <!-- replace --> Something I am studying in public — replace this sentence with
      a real topic.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight">
      Currently exploring
    </h2>
    <p class="text-muted mt-3">
      <!-- replace --> An open question or tool I am poking at. Replace with whatever
      is actually on the desk.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight">Currently reading</h2>
    <p class="text-muted mt-3">
      <!-- replace --> Title, author. Or a paper. Or a spec. Not a performance of
      being well-read.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight">
      Things I am thinking about
    </h2>
    <p class="text-muted mt-3">
      How little software a personal site actually needs, and how to keep
      writing anyway.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
